hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17905","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said, Qatadah narrated to us, from Shahr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, he said, When the plague struck al-Sham, Amr ibn al-As addressed the people and said, This plague is a filth, so disperse from it into these mountain passes and these valleys. That reached Shurahbil ibn Hasanah, so he became angry and came dragging his garment with his sandals hung in his hand, and said, I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Amr is more astray than the donkey of his household. Rather it is the mercy of your Lord, and the supplication of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you."
"17906","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Shurahbil ibn Shufah, he said, The plague occurred, so Amr ibn al-As said, It is a filth, so disperse from it. That reached Shurahbil ibn Hasanah, so he said, I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Amr is more astray than the camel of his household. It is the supplication of your Prophet, and the mercy of your Lord, and the death of the righteous before you. So gather for it and do not disperse from it. That reached Amr ibn al-As, so he said, He spoke the truth."
"17907","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said, Yazid ibn Khumayr informed me, he said, I heard Shurahbil ibn Shufah narrating from Amr ibn al-As that the plague occurred, so Amr ibn al-As said, It is a filth, so disperse from it. And Shurahbil ibn Hasanah said, I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Amr is more astray than the camel of his household, and once Shubah said, more astray than the camel of his household, and that he said, It is the mercy of your Lord, and the supplication of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you. So gather and do not disperse from it. He said, That reached Amr ibn al-As, so he said, He spoke the truth."
"17908","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Abu Munib, that Amr ibn al-As said concerning the plague in the last sermon he gave to the people, This is a filth like a flood; whoever avoids it, it misses him, and like fire; whoever avoids it, it misses him, and whoever stays is burned and harmed by it. So Shurahbil ibn Hasanah said, It is the mercy of your Lord, and the supplication of your Prophet, and the taking of the righteous before you."
